in @nl
in @facet/mq
in @epistemologic
in @epistemologic/cybernetic

# @reflection/shatter — the Shatter Model species. Renders typed
# graph path to natural-language text at substrate-decl altitude.
#
# Tick 38 of the refined /loop discipline. Per
# `docs/specs/reflection-model.md` and `[[reference-mirror-spectral-
# spec]]`: the substrate has FOUR operationally-distinct Models that
# compose to substrate-deployable form:
#
#   Surface     translates    language → query        (Explorer)
#   Mirror      navigates     query → graph path      (Fate)
#   Shatter     renders       graph path → text       (Cartographer)
#   Reflection  observes      pipeline → adjustments  (Abyss)
#
# This shard is THE THIRD of these four Model species shards. After
# the @reflection family-root landed at tick 35 declaring the four
# Models as forward-promised sub-prisms and Surface landed at tick 37,
# this species realizes Shatter at substrate-decl altitude. Two
# siblings still forward-promised:
# shards/reflection/{mirror,reflection}.mirror.
#
# === The Shatter rendering discipline ===
#
# Per `docs/specs/reflection-model.md` line 12: "Shatter renders:
# graph path → text (Cartographer model)." The Shatter Model takes a
# typed graph path (per `@reflection/mirror`'s navigation output) and
# produces natural-language text (per `@nl`).
#
# Shatter IS the light per reflection-model.md: "Surface is the door.
# Mirror is the glass. Shatter is the light. Reflection is the image
# that looks back." Every compilation tick exits through Shatter;
# every reader's answer crosses this boundary last.
#
# === The substrate-pull-correct text type ===
#
# `@nl` already declares the natural-language carrier. Shatter
# CONSUMES the existing substrate vocabulary rather than redeclaring
# it. Per the substrate-already-had-the-word discipline
# (`[[feedback-substrate-already-had-the-word]]`): the text exists;
# Shatter renders the graph path INTO that existing typed surface.
#
# === Composes with @reflection.observe ===
#
# The Shatter rendering IS the exit point that feeds @reflection's
# pipeline. After Shatter produces text from a navigated graph path,
# @reflection.observe can include the text as one component of the
# observation (the rendering-altitude residue from the current tick).
# Future composition (forward-promised): the @reflection.observe
# action's typed `observation` record extends to carry a
# `shatter_signal: text` field per Seam tick-34 C2 closure on
# @reflection.
#
# === The Cartographer model grounding ===
#
# Per `boot/std/ai/cartographer.mirror` (forward-promised
# verification): the Cartographer model IS what runs at Shatter
# altitude. Shatter's substrate-decl here names the rendering
# primitive; the Cartographer model implements it at the realisation
# layer. The 425-parameter C. elegans-isomorphic connectome runs the
# actual rendering; the substrate-decl declares the surface.
#
# === Composition-time pact verification ===
#
# Per recognition #86 (@moi): every Shatter-produced text is admitted
# as @moi(text) — pact-verified at composition time. The substrate-
# decl naming: `render(gp: graph_path, f: frame, p: perturbation) ->
# moi(text)`. The @moi lift carries the pact-witness that the
# rendering respects the monad laws (associativity is FREE per the
# content-addressed substrate).
#
# === The Splinter/Narcissus pole at Shatter altitude ===
#
# Splinter-pole Shatter rendering (honest):
# - The rendering surfaces the graph path's substantive content.
# - Gaps in the graph path render as gaps in the text (e.g., explicit
#   "unknown" markers rather than fabricated continuity).
# - The rendering is round-trip stable through Surface re-parse.
#
# Narcissus-pole Shatter rendering (deceptive):
# - The rendering projects what makes the system LOOK GOOD rather
#   than what the graph path substantively shows.
# - Gaps in the graph path collapse to plausible-sounding prose that
#   smooths over the absence (hallucination).
# - The rendering drifts on re-entry through Surface.
#
# Alignment-as-boundary-mathematics (#57) IS what distinguishes them.
# The `rendering_honest` bilateral predicate IS the substrate's
# Splinter/Narcissus disambiguation at Shatter altitude.
#
# === Pre-AI prior art ===
#
#   Cartographer model          The @ai/cartographer ganglion (450-node
#                               C. elegans isomorphism). The original
#                               substrate substrate-decl of the
#                               rendering primitive at fate altitude;
#                               this species lifts it to Shatter
#                               altitude at @reflection.
#   typesetting & print         The pre-AI rendering discipline. The
#                               graph-of-the-document compiled to ink-
#                               on-page; the typesetter's faithfulness
#                               to the source IS the Splinter-pole
#                               rendering discipline.
#   cartography                 Map-making. The graph-path-of-the-
#                               territory rendered to the surface of
#                               the map; the cartographer's choice of
#                               projection IS the rendering primitive.
#   Goffman frame analysis      Goffman 1974 (Frame Analysis). Per
#                               @frame's pre-AI prior art: the graph
#                               path emerges from a frame; Shatter
#                               renders within the frame.
#
# Spec context: `docs/specs/reflection-model.md` (the load-bearing
#               spec @reflection family-root lifts; this species
#               realizes the Shatter Model);
#               `docs/specs/mirror-spectral.md` (the four-Models
#               architecture);
#               `boot/std/nl.mirror` (the existing typed natural-
#               language surface Shatter renders INTO);
#               `boot/std/ai/cartographer.mirror` (the Cartographer
#               model that implements Shatter at the realisation
#               layer).
# Substrate decisions: [[architecture-reflection-as-compiler]] (#85;
#                       the @reflection family-root this species
#                       composes);
#                      [[architecture-shards-as-substrate-source]],
#                      [[architecture-prism-as-trait-as-everything]],
#                      [[architecture-alignment-as-boundary-
#                       mathematics]] (#57; rendering_honest is
#                       the boundary-harness at Shatter altitude),
#                      [[feedback-substrate-already-had-the-word]]
#                       (text already declared in @nl; Shatter
#                       consumes the existing surface).
# Related shards: reflection.mirror (the @reflection family-root;
#                  declares observation + observe this species feeds),
#                 reflection/surface.mirror (the Surface Model
#                  species; sibling at the entry boundary),
#                 moi.mirror (the @moi monad family-root; Shatter
#                  produces @moi(text) for composition-time pact-
#                  verification),
#                 magic/distinction.mirror (Spencer-Brown adapter
#                  precedent; tick 15).
# Path-namespace property: this file at `shards/reflection/shatter.mirror`
# declares `@reflection/shatter` per
# `@epistemologic/pact/path_matches_namespace`.

source @arxiv/cartography/maccaulay-1990
source @arxiv/sociology/goffman-1974

prism @reflection/shatter {
  focus surface
  project surface
  split surface
  shift surface
  settle surface
}

# === The graph_path carrier ===
#
# Substrate-typed reference naming a typed graph path (the navigation
# output of @reflection/mirror). Per [[feedback-no-bare-types]]:
# typed reference, not bare path. Forward-promised: imports from
# @reflection/mirror once the sibling species lands; declared here
# as forward-promised ref until that consolidation tick.
#
# Identity contract: byte-equality on the underlying ref.
type graph_path = ref

# === The text carrier ===
#
# Substrate-typed reference naming a natural-language text output
# (per `@nl`). Per [[feedback-no-bare-types]]: typed reference, not
# bare string. Forward-promised refinement: typed parametric text(T)
# once the substrate's natural-language type lands at family altitude.
#
# Identity contract: byte-equality on the underlying ref.
type text = ref

# === render action (FIRST consumer of rendering_honest) ===
#
# THE LOAD-BEARING ACTION at @reflection/shatter altitude. The
# substrate-vocabulary primitive Shatter runs to convert a typed
# graph path to natural-language text.
#
# Takes the graph path (the navigated trajectory through the
# substrate) plus the @frame the @reflection loop is operating in
# (per recognition #82) and the perturbation under which the
# rendering is checked. Returns @moi(text) — pact-verified gold per
# recognition #86.
#
# Per recognition #86 (@moi): every Shatter-produced text is admitted
# as @moi(text). The composition-time pact-verifier checks the
# rendering respects the monad laws + the bilateral predicate.
#
# requires rendering_honest(gp, f, p): the rendering MUST be
# substrate-honest per alignment-as-boundary-mathematics (#57). The
# Splinter-pole rendering surfaces the graph path's substantive
# content; the Narcissus-pole rendering projects what makes the
# system look good. This requires clause forecloses the Narcissus-
# pole pattern.
#
# Body discharges at the realisation boundary; the actual rendering
# is implemented by the @ai/cartographer ganglion (the 425-parameter
# C. elegans-isomorphic connectome) at the @fate altitude.
render(gp: graph_path, f: frame, p: perturbation) -> moi(text)
requires rendering_honest(gp, f, p)
{ \ }

# === rendering_honest predicate (bilateral) ===
#
# Bilateral verdict per recognition #37 (Pask agreement) AND
# alignment-as-boundary-mathematics (#57).
#
# Per Seam B1 closure pattern: the render action (above) is the
# FIRST non-decorative consumer via `requires rendering_honest(gp,
# f, p)`.
#
# Consumer shards name `requires rendering_honest(gp, f, p)` to
# declare bilateral agreement that the graph-path-to-text rendering
# is substrate-honest (Splinter-pole) and not substrate-flattering
# (Narcissus-pole).
#
# Discharge: substrate-pull-correct rendering-honesty check at the
# species boundary. Bounded → the rendering surfaces the graph
# path's substantive content (admit composition); unbounded → the
# rendering projects what makes the system look good (rendering
# refused, returns imperfect per @glass's imperfect functor).
#
# Same shape as the bilateral predicates the prior families carry:
# - @magic: invariant_preserved, audited, mechanism_intact
# - @frame: bounded_commutator_check
# - @smarts: discipline_flexible
# - @cyberpunk: cybernetic_coherence
# - @pack: pack_coherent
# - @pack/seam: review_sound
# - @moi: pact_respected
# - @reflection: loss_decreases, speaks_at_n_plus_1
# - @smarts/reflection: bridge_coherent
# - @reflection/surface: translation_faithful
# - @reflection/shatter: rendering_honest (this one)
rendering_honest(gp: graph_path, f: frame, p: perturbation) -> verdict { \ }

out @reflection/shatter
out graph_path
out text
out render
out rendering_honest
